{
  "season": 1,
  "week": 14,
  "articles": [
    {
      "id": "injury-report-s1-w14",
      "type": "feature",
      "author": "ellis-quill",
      "title": "Injury Report: Sunyshore loses Gardener and FLOAT SZN before Rustboro",
      "dek": "Canalave adds another rushing absence; Fortree and Pewter suffer long defensive losses; the full league recovery comparison.",
      "teams": [
        "sunyshore",
        "canalave",
        "fortree",
        "pewter",
        "ecruteak",
        "mossdeep"
      ],
      "frontPageOrder": 9,
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Sunyshore loses two contributors before Rustboro"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Serp Gardener is newly listed out two weeks and FLOAT SZN one after Sunyshore’s 17–0 win over Canalave. The Starseekers host Rustboro next, then visit Mossdeep. Those reported durations make the next two matchups a useful planning horizon, although an actual return still requires confirmation. The injury entries establish availability changes, not a new starting order or the exact play on which either injury occurred."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Sunyshore’s shutout deserves credit on its own terms. Karson Jones now has to prepare for an 8–5 Rustboro club with a changed cornerback group and one fewer available rushing option. Gardener is a cornerback; FLOAT SZN is a halfback. The two absences affect different jobs, so a single broad statement about being short-handed would obscure the decisions the team actually needs to make."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Canalave’s rushing absences grow"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Nidoking is newly out one week after the Sunyshore game. Gabite’s existing absence has counted down from fourteen weeks to thirteen. Canalave now hosts unbeaten Mossdeep after scoring no points last week. The reported injuries add to the difficulty of finding enough rushing production to support the passing game. The evidence confirms the unavailable players; it does not identify a replacement starter."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Olivine has two new offensive absences before hosting Vermilion: halfback Gabite is out one week and receiver Maractus two. Beedrill’s earlier long absence now stands at sixteen weeks. The Ironclads scored twenty-one at Blackthorn but allowed forty-one, so the injury changes arrive alongside work on both sides of the ball. Olivine’s Gabite and Canalave’s Gabite are separate players with different injury entries."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Defensive losses across the league"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Sootopolis cornerback Kingdra is newly out five weeks after the 24–17 loss to Dewford. Fortree outside linebacker Banette has a new twelve-week absence, the longest new entry this week, while receiver Haunter is out four weeks. Pewter outside linebacker Mightyena is out nine weeks and tight end Heatmor two after the 17–9 win at Vermilion. These are new reported absences rather than routine recovery countdowns."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Lavender’s Dugtrio is out one week at cornerback before Celadon visits. Cianwood receiver Haunter is out five weeks after the win at Violet. Mahogany tight end Golduck is out four weeks ahead of Pewter. The two Haunter entries belong to different players and clubs; Fortree’s number 17 and Cianwood’s number 14 should remain distinct in any discussion of replacements."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Recovery updates and minor entries"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Mr. Clanky’s counter has reached zero at Lavender. Frosmoth played quarterback in the win over Azalea, and the cleared recovery counter does not by itself establish which passer will receive the next start. Pastoria’s Oinkologne, Sandygast and receiver Watchog also moved from one reported week to zero. They should not be confused with the separate Watchog who carried eighteen times in Pastoria’s latest game."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Other counters reaching zero belong to Violet’s Barbaracle and Snorlax, Cerulean’s Vikavolt and Raticate, Sootopolis’s Heatmor, Oreburgh’s Huntail, Olivine’s Kabutops, Blackthorn’s Furret, Canalave’s Kecleon and Azalea’s Doduo. A zero counter is an availability update. The recorded game reports establish appearances separately, and the next role remains a team decision."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Mossdeep has a new minor entry for Gronkaludon with zero weeks reported after he caught six passes for sixty-one yards and a touchdown against Petalburg. Ninjaskamara remains out two weeks, Richard Furman three, Marshall Flock one and Luvrelle Revis one. Those four continuing absences have counted down from the previous issue. The new Gronkaludon entry should not be described as another multiweek loss."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The table includes new entries, continuing designations, recovery changes and cleared designations across the league. Durations are the reported remaining weeks after Week 14. No questionable or doubtful labels, medical diagnoses or guaranteed return dates have been added."
        },
